  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Plasma nitriding Ti-6Al-4V at approximately 800°C in a nitrogen-hydrogen glow discharge for 4–6 hours will form a nitrided surface layer.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The nitrided surface layer will consist mainly of TiN.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The treatment will produce a nitrogen-enriched alpha-Ti zone.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At the treatment temperature, nitrogen will diffuse into the Ti-6Al-4V surface.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Diffused nitrogen will react with titanium to form TiN.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nitrogen dissolved in alpha-Ti will produce solid-solution strengthening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "TiN formation and nitrogen solid-solution strengthening will impede dislocation motion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The nitrided layer will increase the surface hardness of Ti-6Al-4V by approximately two to three times relative to untreated Ti-6Al-4V.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The nitrided layer will significantly reduce the pin-on-disk wear rate relative to untreated Ti-6Al-4V.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The hardness and wear improvements will persist under cyclic mechanical loading and pin-on-disk test conditions.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The improvement will be confined primarily to the surface region.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Excessive thermal exposure may alter the bulk microstructure or compromise the ductility and overall mechanical properties of Ti-6Al-4V.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
